  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "good-card-draw-bad-card-draw",
      "title": {
        "en": "Good card draw, bad card draw"
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1003_srt2",
              "name": "Amp Therapy",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1003_srt4",
              "name": "G Chord",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1003_uni2",
              "name": "Soul Riff",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Nia Elasticity, Decibel Rhythm Boost and Activate"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Nia has 2 Unique buffs, Elasticity and Decibel, both activated on Discard\nElasticity is a small Heal that is activated whenever any Ally Extra Attacks\nAllies include Self\nDecibel is a buff that makes every Ally Extra Attack after you Shuffle\nDamage Scales per Decibel stack Nia has\nExtra Attacks from Nia include Decibel, Mute Accent, G Chord, Soul Rip\nThe Extra Attack Damage scales off of the Character that performs it\nActivate is the main Keyword of G Chord, it means to Play the Card for Free\nEnemy turn count still decreases because a Card was Played\nRhythm Boost is the final Unique Buff, available after E2\nIt gives all Allies Additive Damage Increase\nYou get Rhythm Boost by Shuffling the Deck\nShuffles happen whenever you Draw from an empty Draw pile\nShuffles also happen if a card of the type you want to draw is in Discard\nIt will Shuffle your Discard in to gurantee you'll be able to Draw that card\n\"Move\" Never Shuffles the deck"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1003_uni3",
              "name": "Adagio",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "n_0115",
              "name": "Reorganize",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            },
            {
              "cardId": "c_1003_col",
              "name": "Charm",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Nia has very good card draw in Adagio 5\nBecause it Tutors for cards of a specific character\nThe only problem with that is, its not card positive\nExample situation:\n5 Card hand, you use Adagio 5\nAdagio use + discard 1 = 3 cards, Adagio effect brings you back up to 5\nEffectively you went +0 cards, sometimes this can be bad\nExample 2:\n2 Cards in hand, Adagio 5 + Good card\nIf you use the good card you're left with 1 card in hand\nAt that point Adagio 5 can no longer be used\nThis problem comes along with all of Nia's Adagio's some versions card negative\nAdding Neutrals like Reorganize or Gearbag go card positive\nSome characters also like having 10 cards in hand, Adagio is not good at that"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "card-list",
          "items": [
            {
              "cardId": "c_1005_uni1",
              "name": "Target Spotted",
              "note": {
                "en": ""
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Adagio and Eternal Hunger is BROKEN (Attunement)"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "body": {
            "en": "Eternal Hunger has Attunement Draw 1, AP 1\nAttunement Activates when the Card is Drawn\nAdagio is capable of Drawing Eternal Hungers, then Placing them on Top Deck\nAdagio + Eternal Hunger looping means ALOT of Positive Draw and AP\nIf it comes down to it, Nia is still capable of Discarding Eternal Hunger\nAnd Reusing it the Conventional way"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
